post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> OpenCE does not include the game data. You need an Xbox disc image
    (.iso or .xiso) of Halo: Combat Evolved, any region.
==> Run "opence". At the first start it asks for the disc image and copies
    maps/ from it into ~/.local/share/opence.
==> Everything is in ~/.local/share/opence: your settings (config.toml),
    maps/, saves/ (saved games, profiles and the map cache), the log
    (debug.txt) and screenshots.
==> Settings and controls: /usr/share/doc/opence/LINUX.md
EOF
}
